      "hints": [
        "Set $y = 3(x-2)^2 + 2$ and isolate $(x-2)^2$.",
        "Take the positive square root since $x \\ge 2$.",
        "Solve for $x$ and state $f^{-1}(x)$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set $y = 3(x - 2)^2 + 2$ and rearrange to isolate $(x - 2)^2$:\n$$y - 2 = 3(x - 2)^2 \\implies (x - 2)^2 = \\frac{y - 2}{3}$$",
        "Take the positive square root since the domain is $x \\ge 2$:\n$$x - 2 = \\sqrt{\\frac{y - 2}{3}} \\implies x = \\sqrt{\\frac{y - 2}{3}} + 2$$",
        "Swap variables to state $f^{-1}(x)$:\n$$f^{-1}(x) = \\sqrt{\\frac{x - 2}{3}} + 2$$"
      ],
